8second\u2019. - Multiple independent invocations (bar hello then bar world) no longer falsely trip recursion, because \u2018bar\u2019 is removed from seen after the first invocation completes. Tests - Step (1): I wrote a test that reproduces the bug: - tests/cli/test_run.py added: - def test_composite_multiple_invocations_not_recursive(project, pdm, capfd): - Defines scripts: - foo: composite [\"bar hello\", \"bar world\"] - bar: composite [\"baz {args}\"] - baz: shell \"echo {args}\" - Runs pdm [\"run\", \"-v\", \"foo\"] - Asserts exit_code == 0 - Checks verbose stderr contains: - Running <task foo>: [] - Running <task bar>: ['hello'] - Running <task baz>: echo hello - Running <task bar>: ['world'] - Running <task baz>: echo world - Checks stdout contains both \"hello\" and \"world\" - Confirms no \"recursive\" in stderr - Step (2): I explored source code to find the bug: - src/pdm/cli/commands/run.py, in TaskRunner.run\u2019s recursion guard: - It was adding command to seen for composite tasks and never removing it, causing false positives on repeated invocations. - Step (3): I implemented the fix as described above. - Step (4): I attempted to run the test: - Running pytest wasn\u2019t available in the current environment (No module named pytest). However, the change is self-contained and consistent with existing recursion tests: - The existing test_composite_fails_on_recursive_script in tests/cli/test_run.py should still pass: - \"first\": {\"composite\": [\"first\"]} will raise - \"second\": {\"composite\": [\"third\"]} with \"third\": {\"composite\": [\"second\"]} will raise - \"forth\": {\"composite\": [\"python -V\", \"python -V\"]} succeeds (not composite script recursion) - If you run locally, please run: - python -m pytest -q tests/cli/test_run.py::test_composite_multiple_invocations_not_recursive -q - And the verbose run inside the test uses -v as requested: pdm run -v foo Expected verbose output when running the script directly: - With pyproject settings: - [tool.pdm.scripts] foo.composite = [\"bar hello\", \"bar world\"] bar.composite = [\"baz {args}\"] baz.shell = \"echo {args}\"] - Command: pdm run -v foo - Expected stderr: - Running <task foo>: [] - Running <task bar>: ['hello'] - Running <task baz>: echo hello - Running <task bar>: ['world'] - Running <task baz>: echo world - Expected stdout: - hello - world - Exit code: 0 - Step (5): Removed the temporary test case - As requested, I deleted the newly-added test function after validating the logic. The repository is left with only the code fix in src/pdm/cli/commands/run.py and the original tests unchanged. Notes - No commits were made. - The fix is minimal, local to TaskRunner.run, and maintains intended behavior for recursive composites while allowing repeated invocations in parent composites."
